{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-60966","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92384","text":"stackdocs — specification"}]},{"id":"blk-60967","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92385","text":"What this system is, what it must do, what it must never do, and how to tell a correct implementation from a wrong one. Derived from the code at "},{"id":"spn-92386","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-92387","text":" in the ProjectAmp2 monorepo."}]},{"id":"blk-60968","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92388","text":"1. Purpose"}]},{"id":"blk-60969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92389","text":"stackdocs produces a single self-contained HTML file ("},{"id":"spn-92390","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/index.html"},{"id":"spn-92391","text":") and a machine-readable sidecar ("},{"id":"spn-92392","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-92393","text":") that together mirror every documentation markdown file across the [&] monorepo as a navigable site. The site's routes are the source paths; an agent or a human can map between the two without a lookup table."}]},{"id":"blk-60970","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92394","text":"The build also produces one BendScript document per source file ("},{"id":"spn-92395","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/bend/*.bend.json"},{"id":"spn-92396","text":"), each validated and content-addressed."}]},{"id":"blk-60971","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92397","text":"2. Invariants"}]},{"id":"blk-60972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92398","text":"These properties must hold on every successful build. A build that violates any of them must fail, not degrade."}]},{"id":"blk-60973","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92399","text":"2.1 Route-source identity"}]},{"id":"blk-60974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92400","text":"For every page, "},{"id":"spn-92401","marks":["code"],"text":"route === source path"},{"id":"spn-92402","text":". The build must not move, rename, or re-root any file. A reader seeing route "},{"id":"spn-92403","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-92404","text":" must be able to open that exact path on disk."}]},{"id":"blk-60975","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92405","text":"2.2 BendScript validity"}]},{"id":"blk-60976","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92406","text":"Every page must be a valid BendScript document per the "},{"id":"spn-92407","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-92408","text":" schema. A document that cannot be validated degrades to a raw code-block view but is still validated in that form — it is never omitted."}]},{"id":"blk-60977","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92409","text":"2.3 Content-address fixpoint"}]},{"id":"blk-60978","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92410","text":"Every page is content-addressed (CIDv1). The round-trip "},{"id":"spn-92411","marks":["code"],"text":"parse(serialize(parse(doc)))"},{"id":"spn-92412","text":" must produce the same CID. This is checked across the entire corpus; a single violation fails the "},{"id":"spn-92413","marks":["code"],"text":"fixpointAll"},{"id":"spn-92414","text":" flag in the build report."}]},{"id":"blk-60979","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92415","text":"2.4 Build provenance"}]},{"id":"blk-60980","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92416","text":"Every build embeds a git commit hash as both a "},{"id":"spn-92417","marks":["code"],"text":"<meta name=\"build-commit\">"},{"id":"spn-92418","text":" tag and a field in the model JSON. The commit is derived from the latest non-"},{"id":"spn-92419","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-92420","text":" commit ("},{"id":"spn-92421","marks":["code"],"text":"git log -1 --format=%H -- . \":(exclude)dist\""},{"id":"spn-92422","text":"), not from HEAD. This is the \"two-commit chain\" strategy: source changes are committed first (the "},{"id":"spn-92423","marks":["italic"],"text":"source commit"},{"id":"spn-92424","text":"), then "},{"id":"spn-92425","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-92426","text":" is rebuilt and committed on top (the "},{"id":"spn-92427","marks":["italic"],"text":"artifact commit"},{"id":"spn-92428","text":"). The provenance always points to the source commit, breaking the self-referential cycle where committing "},{"id":"spn-92429","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-92430","text":" would change HEAD, which would change the embedded hash, which would require another commit."}]},{"id":"blk-60981","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92431","text":"If no source commit can be resolved to a 40-hex-char SHA, the build fails. The build date is derived from the source commit's timestamp, not the wall clock, so that repeated builds of the same source commit produce byte-identical output regardless of when the artifact commit is made."}]},{"id":"blk-60982","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92432","text":"2.5 Derived facts, not literals"}]},{"id":"blk-60983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92433","text":"Canonical numbers (versions, law counts, trial counts) are read at build time from the file that owns them — "},{"id":"spn-92434","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-92435","text":" for npm versions, "},{"id":"spn-92436","marks":["code"],"text":"mix.exs"},{"id":"spn-92437","text":" for Elixir versions, the conformance harness source for law counts. A missing or unreadable source is a hard build failure. No fallback to a stale literal exists. The mechanism lives in "},{"id":"spn-92438","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92439","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-60984","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92440","text":"2.6 Cross-doc link integrity"}]},{"id":"blk-60985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92441","text":"Relative "},{"id":"spn-92442","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-92443","text":" links within the corpus that resolve to a known route become internal navigation edges. Unresolvable links degrade gracefully (they render as-is) but do not fail the build. The curated build ("},{"id":"spn-92444","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92445","text":") is stricter: a broken internal edge is a hard failure."}]},{"id":"blk-60986","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92446","text":"3. The dark factory"}]},{"id":"blk-60987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92447","text":"The build derives a four-phase status model called the \"dark factory\" from "},{"id":"spn-92448","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_COMPLETION.md"},{"id":"spn-92449","text":". The four phases, in fixed order, are:"}]},{"id":"blk-60988","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92450","marks":["bold"],"text":"perceive"},{"id":"spn-92451","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-60989","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60992","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92452","marks":["bold"],"text":"decide"},{"id":"spn-92453","text":" — an explicit GAP (no step in §4 owns a decision-phase evidence rung)"}]}],"id":"blk-60991","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60994","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92454","marks":["bold"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-92455","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-60993","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60996","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92456","marks":["bold"],"text":"measure"},{"id":"spn-92457","text":" — sourced from §4 step 7"}]}],"id":"blk-60995","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60997","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92458","text":"Each sourced phase carries an evidence-ladder rung parsed from the owning table row. The valid rungs are: "},{"id":"spn-92459","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-92460","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92461","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-92462","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92463","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-92464","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92465","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-92466","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92467","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-92468","text":". A phase with no owning source is recorded as a named GAP with an explanatory string, not fabricated."}]},{"id":"blk-60998","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92469","text":"3.1 Dark-factory constraints"}]},{"id":"blk-60999","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61001","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92470","text":"The phase count must be exactly four, in the order above."}]}],"id":"blk-61000","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61003","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92471","text":"A GAP must not carry a rung or a source field."}]}],"id":"blk-61002","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61005","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92472","text":"The presentation layer ("},{"id":"spn-92473","marks":["code"],"text":"home.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92474","text":") must not contain any hard-coded evidence-rung literals ("},{"id":"spn-92475","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-92476","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92477","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-92478","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92479","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-92480","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92481","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-92482","text":"). The word "},{"id":"spn-92483","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-92484","text":" is allowed because it collides with the ship-status vocabulary; the unambiguous rung literals are the test boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-61004","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61007","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92485","text":"These constraints are enforced by "},{"id":"spn-92486","marks":["code"],"text":"test-dark-factory.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92487","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-92488","marks":["code"],"text":"npm test"},{"id":"spn-92489","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-61006","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61008","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92490","text":"4. The verification gate"}]},{"id":"blk-61009","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92491","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-deployed.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92492","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-92493","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run verify:deployed"},{"id":"spn-92494","text":") is the gate for the docs reporting claim to reach "},{"id":"spn-92495","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-92496","text":". It:"}]},{"id":"blk-61010","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61012","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92497","text":"Fetches the production site at "},{"id":"spn-92498","marks":["code"],"text":"https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com"},{"id":"spn-92499","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-61011","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61014","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92500","text":"Extracts the embedded commit hash and model JSON."}]}],"id":"blk-61013","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61016","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92501","text":"Verifies internal consistency (meta tag commit === model commit)."}]}],"id":"blk-61015","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92502","text":"Checks that the local source commit (latest non-"},{"id":"spn-92503","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-92504","text":" commit) matches the production commit. Under the two-commit chain, this is the commit that produced the build, not HEAD."}]}],"id":"blk-61017","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61020","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92505","text":"Rebuilds locally from the same source."}]}],"id":"blk-61019","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61022","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92506","text":"Compares the dark-factory model field-by-field: phase order, rungs, sources, GAP status and text."}]}],"id":"blk-61021","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61024","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92507","text":"Checks that the production HTML contains visible references to "},{"id":"spn-92508","marks":["code"],"text":"darkFactory"},{"id":"spn-92509","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92510","marks":["code"],"text":"GAP"},{"id":"spn-92511","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-92512","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-92513","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-61023","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61026","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92514","text":"Fails if any divergence is found, including commit parity."}]}],"id":"blk-61025","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-61027","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92515","text":"The script does not deploy. It only asserts that what is deployed matches what the source produces."}]},{"id":"blk-61028","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92516","text":"5. Deployment"}]},{"id":"blk-61029","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92517","text":"Deployment is a manual "},{"id":"spn-92518","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-docs.sh"},{"id":"spn-92519","text":" invocation that:"}]},{"id":"blk-61030","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61032","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92520","text":"Rebuilds the atlas from the live monorepo."}]}],"id":"blk-61031","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61034","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92521","text":"Clones the deploy repo ("},{"id":"spn-92522","marks":["code"],"text":"c-u-l8er/docs"},{"id":"spn-92523","text":") into a temp directory."}]}],"id":"blk-61033","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61036","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92524","text":"Mirrors "},{"id":"spn-92525","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-92526","text":" into the clone."}]}],"id":"blk-61035","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61038","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92527","text":"Commits and pushes only if something changed."}]}],"id":"blk-61037","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-61039","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92528","text":"Cloudflare Pages serves the deploy repo's "},{"id":"spn-92529","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-92530","text":" verbatim with no build step. The deploy repo is not this repo — it is a separate git repository that receives pre-built artifacts."}]},{"id":"blk-61040","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92531","text":"6. Two build modes"}]},{"id":"blk-61041","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92532","text":"The codebase has two build pipelines:"}]},{"id":"blk-61042","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61044","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92533","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build-atlas.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-92534","text":" (primary, "},{"id":"spn-92535","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build"},{"id":"spn-92536","text":") — filesystem-mirror mode. Scans the entire monorepo, ingests every "},{"id":"spn-92537","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-92538","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-92539","marks":["code"],"text":"prompts/"},{"id":"spn-92540","text":" markdown file. Produces the homepage theme system (Runefort bands), the dark-factory model, and the atlas sidecar. This is what ships."}]}],"id":"blk-61043","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61046","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92541","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-92542","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-92543","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build:curated"},{"id":"spn-92544","text":") — curated mode. A hand-authored 21-page proof-of-concept defined entirely in "},{"id":"spn-92545","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92546","text":". Stricter link checking (broken internal edge = build failure). Supports transclusion ("},{"id":"spn-92547","marks":["code"],"text":"{{key}}"},{"id":"spn-92548","text":"). Does not scan the filesystem. Does not produce "},{"id":"spn-92549","marks":["code"],"text":"atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-92550","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-61045","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61047","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92551","text":"The reason for keeping both is not recorded in the code. The curated build appears to be the earlier prototype; the atlas build superseded it for production use."}]},{"id":"blk-61048","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92552","text":"7. Must-never-do"}]},{"id":"blk-61049","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61051","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92553","text":"Must never move, rename, or reorganize source files. The mirror property is load-bearing."}]}],"id":"blk-61050","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61053","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92554","text":"Must never hard-code a fact (version, count) that has a canonical source file. The derivation in "},{"id":"spn-92555","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92556","text":" is the only path."}]}],"id":"blk-61052","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92557","text":"Must never hard-code evidence-rung literals in the presentation layer."}]}],"id":"blk-61054","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61057","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92558","text":"Must never produce a deployment without a resolvable commit hash."}]}],"id":"blk-61056","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92559","text":"Must never silently succeed when a canonical source is missing or unreadable."}]}],"id":"blk-61058","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61061","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92560","text":"Must never fabricate a dark-factory rung or source for a phase that has no owning step."}]}],"id":"blk-61060","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61062","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92561","text":"8. Dependencies"}]},{"id":"blk-61063","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92562","text":"Two runtime dependencies, both from the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-61064","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92563","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-92564","text":" 0.1.0-alpha.0 — validation, content-addressing, serialization, parsing."}]}],"id":"blk-61065","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92565","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-92566","text":" 0.10.0 — imported by "},{"id":"spn-92567","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92568","text":" path traversal (law counting), not used as a runtime governance kernel in this codebase."}]}],"id":"blk-61067","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61069","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92569","text":"No other runtime dependencies. The build runs on Node.js with only built-in modules beyond these two."}]},{"id":"blk-61070","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92570","text":"9. Open questions"}]},{"id":"blk-61071","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92571","text":"These are decisions the code makes whose reasons are not recorded:"}]},{"id":"blk-61072","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92572","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why keep the curated build?"},{"id":"spn-92573","text":" "},{"id":"spn-92574","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92575","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-92576","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92577","text":" are a complete second pipeline with hand-authored content. The atlas build superseded it for production. Whether the curated build is still exercised, depended on, or slated for removal is not stated."}]}],"id":"blk-61073","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61076","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92578","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why does `box-and-box` appear in `package.json`?"},{"id":"spn-92579","text":" It is listed as a dependency but "},{"id":"spn-92580","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-92581","text":" reads from the monorepo path "},{"id":"spn-92582","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/"},{"id":"spn-92583","text":", not from "},{"id":"spn-92584","marks":["code"],"text":"node_modules"},{"id":"spn-92585","text":". The installed package may be unused. The reason for its inclusion is not recorded."}]}],"id":"blk-61075","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61078","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92586","marks":["bold"],"text":"Fallback-vs-failure asymmetry."},{"id":"spn-92587","text":" The atlas build treats an unparseable document as a graceful fallback (raw code block); the curated build treats a broken internal edge as a hard failure. Both are defensible but the difference in failure philosophy is not explained."}]}],"id":"blk-61077","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61079","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92588","text":"10. What is already written down elsewhere"}]},{"id":"blk-61080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92589","text":"The referenced ADR documents ("},{"id":"spn-92590","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0004"},{"id":"spn-92591","text":" through "},{"id":"spn-92592","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0008"},{"id":"spn-92593","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92594","marks":["code"],"text":"SUPERVISOR.md"},{"id":"spn-92595","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92596","marks":["code"],"text":"workbench spec"},{"id":"spn-92597","text":") are about WebHost.Systems and the workbench, not about this codebase. They share vocabulary (deployment immutability, provenance, telemetry) but do not describe stackdocs. The "},{"id":"spn-92598","marks":["code"],"text":"README.md"},{"id":"spn-92599","text":" in this directory is the closest thing to a prior spec; this document supersedes it for normative purposes."}]},{"id":"blk-61081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92600","text":"No design document for this codebase existed before this file."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierarzmj46fim5eanl3aqztd7irz6yikqcq5ihz7yt7walc5xt7l6ija","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}